posted June 27, 2001 04:13 PM &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_profile&u=00000001" target=_blank>
<IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/profile_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Profile for Sleethr"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com" target=_new><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/homepage.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Author's Homepage"></A> &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/priv_message.gif" BORDER='0' ALT="Send New Private Message"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=edit_post&f=4&t=000006&reply_num=000000&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/edit_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Edit/Delete Post"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=reply&f=4&t=000006&replyto=000000"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/quote_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Reply With Quote"></A>
</FONT>
<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
I got to play Verser some more this weekend and I learned a few things about the bard class. Seeing how we have 2-3 active bards in the guild. Brinne, Floot and sometimes Verser, I thought I would share some experience and lessons learned from this weekend.<P><B>ANGSTLICH's APPALLING SCREECH</B><BR>Level: 26<BR>Effect: Fear<BR>Skill: Brass<BR>Target: Area effect<P>Wow, I really did NOT expect this song to work so well. We fought Gornit and when Gornit was 5 levels red or less to Verser, this song would stick about 90% of the time. I would just turn this song on after Nef had snared Gornit and we could fear kite Gornit with almost no effort.<P><B>SOLON's SONG OF THE SIRENS</B><BR>Level: 27<BR>Effect: Charm<BR>Skill: Wind<BR>Target: Single<P>Okay, this one takes a TON of practice and I'm still working on my methods, but with it, I was solo'ing white to low red cons in The Over There. I was VERY surprised at what I could effectivly charm with this song. ( CHA 111 ) I was expecting to have trouble with blues, not much, but expected 50% or more resists. Wrong, against a blue, I got about 90% success rate, maybe more. Versus whites and yellows, about 70% and low reds, about 50%. These are all guess-ta-ments, but should be close. <P>Now, yer saying only 50% success against reds or yer saying WOW, he could charm a red. Either way, 50% doesn't sound good enough to be effective. However; I could twist selo's and charm almost constantly to keep a mob charmed or re-charm and stay outta the mad mobs reach with ease. <P>One problem that I had is with mobs that were very mad at me from charming and my new pet not being able to taunt it enough to get it to stop chasing me. I think I ran around for 15 minutes on time with a pissed of ex-pet chasing me with a new-charmed pet trying to hit the old pet. That doesn't work so well.  <IMG SRC="frown.gif" border="0"> You would think that the new pet would be beating the snot out of the old pet while chasing it around, but it didn't work that way. <P>Targeting is a pain though. Especially when you have so little time to pick swap targets. I would sometimes hit the un-charmed target with the snare/slow song to help my pet take less damage. I recently read that a song will hit the target you had targeted when you first start the song. It takes 3 seconds for a song's effect to proc after you hit the button. <P>Here's how it worked:<P>1) Target mob1 and charm.<BR>2) Target mob2 and /pet attack<BR>3) F1 F1 to retarget mob1/pet<BR>3) hit selo's  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Charm doesn't last too long so I wouldn't start the tricky stuff until after I got mob1 attacking mob2. However; mob1/pet remembers last command when you re-charm.<P>2nd round and rest depending on how tricky you wanna get.<P>1) Charm breaks on mob1<BR>2) recharm or selo's, keeping selo's up is a must.<BR>3) soon as mob1 re-charmed, target mob2 and hit snare or DD song button.<BR>4) F1 F1 to retarget pet.<BR>5) 3 seconds later, Snare or DD song will hit mob2, NOT your current target.<BR>6) selo's  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Rinse and repeat.<P>I was getting anywhere from 1/2 to 1 blue bubble of exp per mob. Sometimes I would get lucky and both mobs would beat themselves up so bad that when charm broke they would both go into flee mode. I'd just snare mob1 and kill, then snare mob2 and kill. That was the best exp senerio. <P>I would usually have mob1 kill mob2 and then I had to go find mob3 to charm to kill mob1/ex-pet. That got into trouble with mob3 not being able to taunt mob1 and hit the thing either due to mob1 chasing me all over the place.<P>I think getting a SoW ( even though it's slower then selo's ) might help with the kiting a little more. Not having to twist that song in would make things much easier.<P>30th level targeted DoT song might make this process a tad easier too. Hitting mob2 with the chant song could help more.<P> <BR>Ghall   posted 02-19-2001 09:03 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Actually Sleethr I'd try charming one mob over and over again until it has slain 3 or 4 mobs and is about to die .. then I would kill my pet .. rinse and repeat.<BR>no need to waste a good pet and minutes of running around hoping your new pet can taunt your ex-pet off of you. With SoW you'd be able to work things a little better and allow your pet to kill more NPC's. I feel that tactic would work better, especially if you can manage to charm red NPC's<BR> <BR>Brod and Shato   posted 02-19-2001 09:35 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Gotta spend some time camping AC. I've seen plenty of bards and druids with j-boots. Bards because it frees up a song slot, and it allows them to twist in an additional song. Druids because if they are kiting something tough/fast they can refresh j-boot on the run. <P>Sleethr   posted 03-29-2001 03:51 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Rich has way too much time on his hands at work so here is what I cooked up. Hope you all like it.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><BR> <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~rwn7734/div13/VersersBardGuideV1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~rwn7734/div13/VersersBardGuideV1.htm</A><P>--------------------<P>Sleethr Dragynthorn
</FONT>
